        "kicker": "Our namesake",
        "headline": "Mamik Olnian",
        "body": "<p>Mamik was the one everyone came to. A sore back, a long week, a new baby, bad news. Somehow you ended up in her kitchen, and you left better than you arrived. She never called any of it wellness. She called it feeding people properly and paying attention.</p><p>She was exacting about ingredients in a way that seemed excessive right up until you tasted the difference. Nothing cheap. Nothing she couldn't name. Nothing bought only because it happened to be on sale that week. She would rather make less of something than make it with the wrong thing in it.</p><p>We started OLNIAN because that standard wasn't anywhere on the supplement shelf. Beautiful labels, ingredient lists as long as your arm, and very little you'd actually want to hand to someone you love. So we built the company she would have been willing to put her name on, which, in the end, is exactly what we did.</p>",
